{title: Quemadmodum Desiderat Cervus}
{subtitle: Psalms 42:2–4}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Quemadmodum desiderat cervus ad fontes aquarum
ita desiderat anima mea ad te, Deus
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Sitivit anima mea ad Deum fortem, vivum
quando veniam [C]et appa[Gm]rebo [Dm]ante [C]faciem [Gm]De[Dm]i
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Fuerunt mi[C]hi lacri[Gm]mae panes di[Bb]e ac noc[C]te
dum di[Dm]citur mihi qu[C]otidi[Gm]e: u[Dm]bi est [C]Deus tu[Gm]us
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Dm]ad te, De[C][Gm][Bb][C][Dm]us
{end_of_verse}
